[00:40] orchestrator     directive 1 from steer: Pair-correlation route. Verified outside the container against a brute oracle for k = F_n - 1 up to n=12; reproduce it here before building on it. Write the square of a factor value as a double sum over digit positions: Psi(k) = sum over j,jp of C(j,jp) * 10^(2k-2-j-jp), where C(j,jp) counts the length-k factors carrying a 1 at both positions j and jp. At k = F_n - 1 the k+1 factors are the F_n rotations of the standard word q_n truncated to k letters, so the sum over factors is a sum over rotations and C(j,jp) = A(jp-j), the CYCLIC autocorrelation of q_n, a function of the lag alone. A has an exact closed form: A(d) = max(0, m - t) + max(0, m - (N - t)) with N = F_n = length of q_n, m = number of ones in q_n, t = (d*m) mod N. Checked for every lag at n=3..12, and Psi(F_n - 1) = sum over j,jp of A(jp-j)*10^(2k-2-j-jp) reproduces the brute Psi exactly there. For a fixed lag the inner sum over j is geometric, so Psi collapses to ONE sum over lags of A(d) times an explicit geometric weight, and what is left is sum over d of (a*d mod N) * x^d mod M, a Euclidean/Ostrowski recursion costing O(log N), not 10^18 terms. Directive 2 gives a stronger form of this that removes the k = F_n - 1 restriction; read both before choosing.
