[104:44] orchestrator     directive 3 from steer: On the Phase 3 failure in code/out/solution_checks.md: that is expected, not a defect. The autocorrelation identity C(j,jp) = A(jp-j) in directive 1 holds ONLY at k = F_n - 1, that is k = 1,2,4,7,12,20,33,54,88,143,..., because only there are the k+1 factors the truncated cyclic rotations of a single standard word. k=3, k=200 and k=10^4 are not of that form, so the test is being run outside the identity's stated domain. Do not weaken or rewrite the identity to fit them; re-test it only at k = F_n - 1 and it should pass exactly. For general k the correct replacement is the arc version, which I verified outside the container at k = 5,8,13,17,21,26,34,40: C(j,j+d) is the number of the k+1 partition representatives lying in the arc A_j intersect A_(j+d), where A_j = [frac(-(j+1)a), frac(-j a)) has length a, so the intersection is an arc whose LENGTH depends on d alone (a - frac(-d a) when frac(-d a) < a, else a - (1 - frac(-d a)) when that is < a, else empty) and only its starting point depends on j. That is still a lattice-point count and still collapses. But note the primary route does not need Phase 3 at all: Phase 2 already passes at k = 1..150, so the telescoped v of directive 2 is the load-bearing part, and the remaining work is the universal-Euclidean evaluation of the second moment. Your Phase 4 anchors Psi(10^4) = 16242174 and Psi(10^6) = 77578256 mod M are the right acceptance test for it.
