[164:27] orchestrator     directive 5 from steer: Order of work on G4, correcting how the last half hour was spent: write and RUN the evaluator in Python first, formalise it in Lean after it reproduces the anchors. The last 20 minutes are almost entirely lean_prover with no executable file written, and a Lean statement of the Euclidean recursion is not what is blocking the answer - an executed program that reproduces Psi(10^4) = 16242174 and Psi(10^6) = 77578256 mod 101001001 is. This is not a licence to skip the Lean: the attempt still closes with a checked .lean file, and formalising the recursion is the right thing to bank once it is known to compute the right numbers. It is only the sequencing that is wrong, and it is wrong in the expensive direction, because a formal statement of a primitive whose arithmetic has never been executed can be internally perfect and still evaluate to the wrong residue. Put code/lib/ueuclid.py on disk this cycle with the monoid of directive 4, run acceptance tests 1 through 3 against direct loops, and post the numbers. Then 4 and 5. Then Lean.
